      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">Last Updated: October 2026</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Highlight Box -->
    <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-cyan-950/40 border border-cyan-500/30 text-xs sm:text-sm text-cyan-200 leading-relaxed">
      <strong>Agreement Summary:</strong> 3DPrintingCostCalc.com is a free engineering estimation and pricing calculator for 3D printing makers, print farms, and businesses. By accessing our website, you agree to these terms, our calculation disclaimers, and understand that all estimates must be verified against your specific equipment, materials, and operating parameters.
    </div>

    <!-- 1. Acceptance of Terms -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">1. Acceptance of Terms & Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing or using 3DPrintingCostCalc.com (including all subpages, calculators, embedded tools, and downloadable quote templates), you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms of Service and our Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, you must discontinue use of the website immediately.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Nature of the Service -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">2. Nature and Purpose of the Service</h2>
      <p>
        3DPrintingCostCalc.com provides computational utilities designed to estimate additive manufacturing parameters, including raw material costs, electrical energy consumption, machine capital depreciation, maintenance reserves, post-processing labor, and commercial marketplace pricing models. All calculators are provided free of charge for reference, educational, and business estimation purposes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. Technical Calculation Disclaimer -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">3. Technical Calculation Disclaimer & Physical Tolerances</h2>
      <p>
        While our mathematical formulas and slicer parsing algorithms are built according to modern additive manufacturing engineering standards, real-world 3D printing involves numerous physical variables that cannot be fully predicted by browser-based geometry inspection alone:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
        <li><strong>Material Density & Batch Variations:</strong> Polymer densities (e.g., PLA at 1.24 g/cm³, PETG at 1.27 g/cm³, ABS at 1.04 g/cm³) may fluctuate by ±3% to 5% across different filament manufacturers, pigment loadings, and filler contents (e.g., carbon fiber, wood, or glow particles).</li>
        <li><strong>Infill & Geometry Approximations:</strong> Volume estimates from raw STL and OBJ meshes assume uniform internal infill geometries (such as Gyroid, Grid, or Honeycomb). Slicer-generated wall perimeters, solid top/bottom layers, support interface densities, and adaptive layer heights will impact final printed part weight.</li>
        <li><strong>Machine Kinematics & Slicing Acceleration:</strong> Print time estimates derived from G-code headers reflect slicer simulations. Machine-level acceleration, jerk limits, bed leveling routines, nozzle purge cycles, and firmware flow rate ceilings will cause variations in actual cycle durations.</li>
        <li><strong>Resin SLA/DLP Variables:</strong> Liquid photopolymer calculations include estimated support overhead and isopropyl alcohol (IPA) bath depletion. Part orientation, hollowing drain hole efficiency, internal resin entrapment, and FEP release film degradation may influence consumption.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Users are advised to conduct physical test prints and weigh prototypes on calibrated scales to verify baseline values prior to fulfilling high-volume production orders.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Commercial & Financial Disclaimer -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">4. Commercial Pricing, Marketplace Fees & Financial Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Our commercial seller pricing calculators offer suggested retail quotes and breakdown platform fees for third-party marketplaces such as Etsy, eBay, and Shopify.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
        <li>Marketplace fee structures (transaction fees, payment processing fees, listing fees, regulatory operating fees, and currency conversions) change periodically and may vary by geographic territory and seller tier.</li>
        <li>3DPrintingCostCalc.com does not guarantee profitability, business success, or accuracy of third-party fee projections.</li>
        <li>You retain sole legal and commercial responsibility for setting customer prices, collecting appropriate sales taxes/VAT, managing shipping logistics, and fulfilling client contracts.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

